{
  "about": "Google's rich-result types and the properties its feature pages mark required or recommended, read by schema-check.mjs. Built from the search gallery (page updated 2026-10-16) and each feature's page. A rule covers its type and every subtype. Nested lists mean one of these. except: subtypes it skips. under: only when nested in one of these types; as: only through that property. top: only when not nested. standalone: also required when not nested, or nested as `via`. lastMayOmit: the last item of its list may leave that one out. alsoOn: the property may sit on the object in that key. when: only when the item has one of these properties (\"*\": any value). elsewhere: an item with this property may stand for one shown on another page (a forum post on a category page), which Google doesn't hold to the one-of lists in required, so missing them is only a note. needsRating: Google shows the result only with one of these, which must come from real reviews, so it's a note. Recommended lists leave out ratings and reviews (SCHEMA-04) and what Google marks \"if applicable\" or ties to a condition, so a warning never asks for something a page shouldn't have. retired: rich results Google no longer shows, matched by exact type; keep: still worth keeping, never flagged; note: shown with a kept type as information.",
